   "file": "content/FMA_7485/tier1.md",
   "text": "The sternum, or breastbone, anchors the front of the rib cage. This long, flat bone is formed from three bones that fuse in adults. The clavicles, or collarbones, and the first seven ribs connect to the sternum. The front of the heart sits behind the sternum.",
